ch/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:366:        stack.extend(list(f.get('inputs') or []) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on') or [] if r in figs])\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:401:        if kind != 'estimate' and f.get('rests_on'):\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:402:            errors.append(('S7', f'{fid}: rests_on is for estimates only'))\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:423:        for r in f.get('rests_on') or []:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:425:                errors.append(('S7', f'{fid}: rests_on names {r}, which is neither a figure nor a shown passage'))\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:435:        hit = any(cyclic(r) for r in list(f.get('inputs') or []) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on') or [] if r in figs])\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:439:        errors.append(('S7', 'a figure depends on itself (through inputs or rests_on)'))\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:584:                errors.append(('S5', f'{v}: its reference {ref} has no quoted consensus, guidance or outside figure'))\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:595:    \"\"\"[54] The figures the outcomes adopt: each reached from an outcome (inputs and rests_on) with no figure of its own quantity and\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:608:        for r in list(f.get('inputs') or []) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on') or [] if r in figs]:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:739:            rested = {figs[r]['what']['scope'] for r in f.get('rests_on') or [] if r in figs}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:175:- two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:176:  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:35:- **Uses.** A figure *uses* another when the other is among its `inputs`, at any depth. An estimate's `rests_on` is a judgement, not\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:47:| S5 | an own estimate passed off as the market's | The figure marked in `reference_for` and every figure beneath it (inputs and rests_on) is a source, or computed with no basis forecast. None is an estimate. At least one is a quoted consensus, guidance or third_party figure, which may be the marked figure itself. A forecast member has exactly one marked reference figure or a `reference_unavailable` reason. | `reference_for`; `reference_unavailable` |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:49:| S7 | structure: the calculation | Ids are unique and never equal a passage id. `inputs` name figures; `rests_on` names figures or passages. No figure uses itself. A figure has value, or low and high (low ≤ high), never both. A source has `evidence_id` and `quote_number`; a computed figure has `inputs` and `operation`; an estimate has `basis_text`. Basis forecast is never on a source. There is one answer per member. An unresolved answer has `why`, rung null, `reference_unavailable` null and no marked figure. | the field descriptions |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:67:| S4 | two forecasts of one quarter | For each shared quantity the request lists, at most one figure has basis forecast. When a member's outcome uses that quantity, exactly one does, and every figure of that quantity the outcome uses is reached only through it (the forecast itself may be computed from guidance or consensus). | the family header; `basis` |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:68:| S5 | an own estimate passed off as the market's | A figure marked in `reference_for` has, at any depth beneath it, no estimate and no forecast, and at least one source of basis consensus, guidance or third_party. A forecast member has exactly one marked reference figure or a `reference_unavailable` reason. | `reference_for`; `reference_unavailable` |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:70:| S7 | structure: the calculation | Ids are unique. `inputs` name figures and `rests_on` names figures or passages. No figure depends on itself. A figure has value, or low and high (low ≤ high), never both. A source has `evidence_id` and `quote_number`; a computed figure has `inputs` and `operation`; an estimate has `basis_text`. Basis forecast is never on a source. There is one answer per member. An unresolved answer has `why`, no rung, no marked figure and no reference. | the field descriptions |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:90:| `reference_for` | \"The members for which this figure is the market's reference. It and every figure beneath it is a source or a computed figure, never an estimate or a forecast, and at least one of them is a quoted consensus, guidance or outside figure.\" |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:96:- \"Shared quantities: …\" (unchanged list).\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:110:| `basis` | enum reported, guidance, consensus, third_party, forecast | \"reported: an actual; guidance: the company's outlook; consensus: analysts' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family's own forecast, on a computed or estimate figure only.\" |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:120:| `rests_on` | array of strings or null | \"Estimate only: the ids of the figures and passages it rests on.\" |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:122:| `reference_for` | array of member ids (enum) | \"The members for which this figure is the market's reference: a consensus, guidance or outside figure from a shown passage, or one computed only from such figures and reported ones. No estimate or forecast anywhere beneath it.\" |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:137:- \"Shared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure that uses the quantity takes it: …\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:147:  `render_v13.v13s_schema` builds the schema; `judging-v13s.txt` holds the system text.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:156:  those readers read (`evidence`, `inputs`, `rests_on`, `outcome`, `reference`), and the dropped keys never appear.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:175:- **A1, correct forms.** Each passes:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:176:  - a $4.5 billion ± 3% guidance as two sources with apply_growth ends;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:192:- **A2, defects.** Each is refused by its named rule:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:198:  - **S4:** two forecasts of one shared quarter; an outcome reaching guidance for a shared quarter beside the forecast.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:216:- **A1 adds:**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:222:- **A2 adds:**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:226:  - Q3 guidance used directly beside a Q3 forecast (S4);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:252:- **An accepted reply with a named defect** (marked by both readers, or by the third reader) is a stop.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:267:**Stop.** The test stops on any of these:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:268:- an A1 form refused;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:269:- an A2 defect not refused by its rule;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4:- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:6:- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:36:        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.BASES - {'prior_forecast'}), 'description': 'reported: an actual; guidance: the company\\'s '\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:58:        'basis_text': nullable(S), 'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:81:def v13s_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:94:        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['reported', 'guidance', 'consensus', 'third_party', 'forecast'], 'description': \"reported: an \"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:95:                  \"actual; guidance: the company's outlook; consensus: analysts' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this \"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:127:        'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S, 'description': 'Estimate only: the ids of the figures and passages it rests on.'}),\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:133:                              \"consensus, guidance or outside figure. A past period's reported share or multiple carried to another period \"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:154:                            'point a final range rests on, are fine). A growth rate computed from guidance may serve as a stated benchmark for an estimate. '\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:161:def v13s_header(family, shown):\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:177:    lines.append(f'Shared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes: {shared}.')\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:218:        header = v13s_header(family, shown)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:220:        header = (f'Relations: {rel}.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\n'\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
