 str(error))], 'recorded': [], 'published': {}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:559:        norm, recorded, named = card_view(calc, v, checked.get('recorded', []), prefix, checker(fmt))\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:565:             '  Recorded assumptions: ' + json.dumps(recorded),\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_rehearsal.py:195:    ok('the reader card maps the recorded estimate to the card\\'s figure numbers', '\"type\": \"estimate\", \"figure\": \"F' in text, text[:900])\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:45:| S8 | a part added into its whole; periods misadded | A sum never adds a figure that uses (or is) the part's quantity to one that uses (or is) the whole's: the whole already includes the part. A difference may subtract the part from the whole only to give the rest, another scope. When a sum's or difference's inputs are periods of one quantity, each period is written FY2027, FY2027 Q3, FY2027 H1, FY2027 Q1-Q3 (or CY likewise), and together they make up the output's period exactly (Q1 + Q2 = H1; FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4). An estimate that rests on both the part and the whole is recorded for readers. | `operation`; `what.period`; the family header |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:146:  `publish_decision`, `evaluate`, `upstream_of` and `key`, and returns `{errors, recorded, published}` as `calc_check` does.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:158:- The reader brief is unchanged. Its `deciding_gap` question is where readers judge the recorded conversions and estimates.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:179:  - a year-over-year rate on last year's quarter (recorded);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:189:  - a conversion between quantities (recorded);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:224:  - an estimate resting on both part and whole (recorded, not refused, and the record asserted);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:262:  - for each accepted answer, whether each forecast is supported, and whether its recorded conversions or estimates decide its band.\n10957:## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n10961:  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
