{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10957,10996p;11346,11370p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py | sed -n '503,524p'; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/CHECKED.json | sed -n '131,164p'\"","aggregated_output":" 10957\t## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n 10958\t\n 10959\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n 10960\t  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n 10961\t  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n 10962\t- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n 10963\t  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n 10964\t  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n 10965\t  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n 10966\t- **Diagnosis:**\n 10967\t  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n 10968\t     figures.\n 10969\t  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n 10970\t  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n 10971\t  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n 10972\t- **Measured:**\n 10973\t  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n 10974\t  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n 10975\t  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n 10976\t  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n 10977\t  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n 10978\t- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n 10979\t  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n 10980\t  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n 10981\t  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n 10982\t    reference);\n 10983\t  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n 10984\t  - extraction unchanged;\n 10985\t  - families declared for the test.\n 10986\t- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n 10987\t- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n 10988\t  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n 10989\t- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n 10990\t\n 10991\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n 10992\t\n 10993\t- **The questions** (after D725):\n 10994\t  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n 10995\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n 10996\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n 11346\t## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n 11347\t\n 11348\t- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n 11349\t  - 【增速参考】\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\n 11350\t  - 【市场参照】\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\n 11351\t  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\n 11352\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"不算错 (推荐)\"; \"不能 (推荐)\"; \"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\".\n 11353\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11354\t  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\n 11355\t     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\n 11356\t  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\n 11357\t     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\n 11358\t     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\n 11359\t  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\n 11360\t     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\n 11361\t- **How they are applied (D738):**\n 11362\t  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\n 11363\t  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\n 11364\t  - Then three steps:\n 11365\t    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n 11366\t    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\n 11367\t    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\n   503\tdef card_view(calc, view_id, recorded, prefix='', ck=cc):\n   504\t    \"\"\"[47b.3] One card as its own derivation: the figures its outcome and reference rest on, renumbered F1.. (after `prefix`) for this\n   505\t    card alone, and the recorded assumptions about its outcome or its own figures mapped to the same numbers.\"\"\"\n   506\t    figs = {f['id']: f for f in calc['figures']}\n   507\t    refs = lambda f: list(f.get('inputs', [])) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs] + \\\n   508\t        ([f['adjusts']['figure']] if f.get('adjusts') else []) + ([f['bridge']] if f.get('bridge') else [])\n   509\t    ans = next(a for a in calc['answers'] if a['view_id'] == view_id)\n   510\t    own = set()\n   511\t    for start in (ans.get('outcome'), (ans.get('reference') or {}).get('figure')):\n   512\t        if start in figs:\n   513\t            own |= ck._upstream_of(start, figs, refs) | {start}\n   514\t    sub = {'figures': [f for f in calc['figures'] if f['id'] in own], 'answers': [ans]}\n   515\t    norm, rename = normalise(sub, prefix)\n   516\t    mapped = []\n   517\t    for r in recorded:                                    # an assumption about this card's outcome, or about one of its own figures\n   518\t        named = [r[k] for k in ('figure', 'bridge') if isinstance(r.get(k), str)]\n   519\t        if (r.get('outcome') == view_id or any(n in rename for n in named)) and all(n in rename for n in named):\n   520\t            mapped.append({k: rename[v] if k in ('figure', 'bridge') else v for k, v in r.items()})\n   521\t    return norm, mapped, sorted({f['evidence'] for f in sub['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} | set(ans.get('cites', []))\n   522\t                                | {x for f in sub['figures'] for x in f.get('rests_on', []) if str(x).startswith('e')})\n   523\t\n   524\t\n   131\t    388.32032,\n   132\t    null\n   133\t   ]\n   134\t  },\n   135\t  \"decision\": \"publish\"\n   136\t },\n   137\t {\n   138\t  \"case\": \"P-v4\",\n   139\t  \"writer\": \"claude\",\n   140\t  \"sha256\": \"a4afb41bbbdcbce71c54edcf161c9b50139275d5218241a9f0ad4c6c938f1044\",\n   141\t  \"stage\": \"checked\",\n   142\t  \"errors\": [\n   143\t   [\n   144\t    \"S4\",\n   145\t    \"v4: uses F4 for NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3 beside its forecast figure F8\"\n   146\t   ]\n   147\t  ],\n   148\t  \"recorded\": [\n   149\t   {\n   150\t    \"type\": \"conversion between quantities\",\n   151\t    \"figure\": \"F6\"\n   152\t   },\n   153\t   {\n   154\t    \"type\": \"qualified source\",\n   155\t    \"figure\": \"F7\",\n   156\t    \"qualifier\": \"roughly\"\n   157\t   },\n   158\t   {\n   159\t    \"type\": \"estimate\",\n   160\t    \"figure\": \"F8\",\n   161\t    \"assumption\": \"My estimate: the Q3 guidance midpoint of $108.0 billion plus a beat of about 4%. That is smaller than the 5.7% by which Q2 beat its midpoint and below the third-party $113.6 billion (3.1% over the high end of guidance), because supply covers only about 70% of demand and capacity is reported sold out, which limits room for a large upside surprise.\"\n   162\t   },\n   163\t   {\n   164\t    \"type\": \"conversion between quantities\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import copy, json, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nstudy = Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'')\nsys.path[:0] = [str(study), '\\\\''src'\\\\'']\nimport calc_small as cs\nfrom hivemind import model\nimport small_cases as sc\nfolder = Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P-v4'\\\\'')\nitem = json.loads((folder/'\\\\''item.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nsaved = json.loads((folder/'\\\\''answers/claude.json'\\\\'').read_text())\ndef report(label, a, fam, p, s):\n    schema_errors = model.check_schema(a, s)\n    if schema_errors:\n        print(label, '\\\\''schema'\\\\'', schema_errors)\n        return\n    calc = cs.from_answer(a,fam)\n    result = cs.check(fam,p,calc)\n    print(label, cs.publish_decision(fam,calc,result), result['\\\\''errors'\\\\''], result['\\\\''published'\\\\''])\ndef stored(label, a, fam=item['\\\\''family'\\\\'']):\n    report(label, a, fam, item['\\\\''passages'\\\\''], item['\\\\''schema'\\\\''])\ndef fig(a, name):\n    return sc.fig(a, name)\ndef estimated_rate(a, rate, dollars, assumed, value, target, base, text):\n    a['\\\\''figures'\\\\''].append(sc.F(assumed, target, '\\\\''estimate'\\\\'', '\\\\''forecast'\\\\'', '\\\\''%'\\\\'', value=value, basis_text=text, rests_on=[rate]))\n    fig(a,dollars).update(inputs=[base,assumed])\n\nimport types\nblanket = types.ModuleType('\\\\''blanket'\\\\'')\nsrc = study/'\\\\''s4-ratestop-calc_small.py.txt'\\\\''\nexec(compile(src.read_text(), str(src), '\\\\''exec'\\\\''), blanket.__dict__)\ndef compare(label, a):\n    print(label, model.check_schema(a,item['\\\\''schema'\\\\'']))\n    for mod in (cs,blanket):\n        calc = mod.from_answer(a,item['\\\\''family'\\\\''])\n        r = mod.check(item['\\\\''family'\\\\''],item['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],calc)\n        print(mod.__name__,mod.publish_decision(item['\\\\''family'\\\\''],calc,r),r['\\\\''errors'\\\\''],r['\\\\''published'\\\\''])\ndef set_q4(a, value, inputs, op):\n    fig(a,'\\\\''F10'\\\\'').update(value=value,inputs=inputs,operation=op)\n    fig(a,'\\\\''F11'\\\\'')['\\\\''value'\\\\''] = 177.82+112.5+value\n    fig(a,'\\\\''F14'\\\\'')['\\\\''value'\\\\''] = (fig(a,'\\\\''F11'\\\\'')['\\\\''value'\\\\'']/215.9-1)*100\na = copy.deepcopy(saved)\nmul = 108/96.2\nfig(a,'\\\\''F9'\\\\'').update(inputs=['\\\\''F4'\\\\'','\\\\''F2'\\\\''],operation='\\\\''ratio'\\\\'',unit='\\\\''x'\\\\'',value=mul)\nset_q4(a,96.2*mul*mul,['\\\\''F2'\\\\'','\\\\''F9'\\\\'','\\\\''F9'\\\\''],'\\\\''product'\\\\'')\ncompare('\\\\''round 56 repeated multiple'\\\\'',a)\na = copy.deepcopy(saved)\nfig(a,'\\\\''F9'\\\\'').update(inputs=['\\\\''F8'\\\\'','\\\\''F4'\\\\''],value=-4)\na['\\\\''figures'\\\\''].append(sc.F('\\\\''START'\\\\'',sc.W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027 Q3'\\\\'','\\\\''revenue run-rate'\\\\''),'\\\\''computed'\\\\'','\\\\''forecast'\\\\'','\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',value=108,inputs=['\\\\''F8'\\\\'','\\\\''F9'\\\\''],operation='\\\\''apply_growth'\\\\''))\na['\\\\''figures'\\\\''].append(sc.F('\\\\''G12'\\\\'',sc.W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027 Q4'\\\\'','\\\\''revenue sequential growth'\\\\''),'\\\\''estimate'\\\\'','\\\\''forecast'\\\\'','\\\\''%'\\\\'',value=12,basis_text='\\\\''roughly 12 percent forward growth'\\\\''))\nset_q4(a,108*1.12,['\\\\''START'\\\\'','\\\\''G12'\\\\''],'\\\\''apply_growth'\\\\'')\ncompare('\\\\''round 56b cancellation'\\\\'',a)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
